  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "6.7.8.2, client-only fixes against Firefly III API 6.7.8. Clearing a stored value: an update leaves out a null field, so the server keeps what it has; the new ClearedFields.Clear extension (update.Clear(u => u.TargetDate)) sets a field to null and sends it as null, so a piggy bank's target, a recurrence's end, a tag's date or location, a bill's end and extension dates or a split's optional dates can be removed. Breaking: BillUpdate.EndDate and ExtensionDate are DateTime? (they could never be null). RuleTriggerUpdate gains Prohibited, which the spec leaves out: an edited rule lost its NOT triggers. 6.7.8.1: requests send only what the caller set; the bool/int fields of the *Update models are bool?/int?; *Store active defaults to true; piggy banks send account_id and a currency; responses read numbers as strings, date-times as dates and a null budget CurrencyDecimalPlaces; CategoryUpdate.Notes and Color are three-state.",
